    {
      "title": "TLS Inside EAP",
      "desc": "The server proves who it is",
      "detail": "The laptop and the server now run a TLS 1.3 handshake inside EAP; the access point repacks each message, EAPOL over the air and RADIUS on the wire. The server sends its certificate and asks for the laptop’s. The laptop checks that it was issued by the company’s own certificate authority to radius.example.org. That check is what stops a fake access point from catching the login.",
      "facts": [
