    {
      "title": "Why Enterprise",
      "desc": "One account per person",
      "detail": "When someone leaves, their account is disabled and nobody else changes a password. Every login gets its own keys, so users can’t read each other’s traffic, and the RADIUS server records who connected and when. eduroam works the same way: a visitor’s login for user@their-university is passed from RADIUS server to RADIUS server until it reaches their own university.",
      "facts": [
